1
00:06:06,666 --> 00:06:12,666
What If You Could Feel Like They Do... We Can Help.

2
00:12:13,333 --> 00:12:19,333
Antiviral is a science fiction, horror film directed by Brandon Cronenberg.

3
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Syd March is an employee at a clinic that sells injections of live
viruses harvested from sick celebrities to obsessed fans.

4
00:24:26,666 --> 00:24:32,666
When he becomes infected with the disease that kills super sensation Hannah
Geist, Syd becomes a target for collectors and rabid fans.

5
00:30:33,333 --> 00:30:39,333
He must unravel the mystery surrounding her death
before he suffers the same fate.

6
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:46,000
Syd March, played by Caleb Landry Jones.

7
00:42:46,666 --> 00:42:52,666
Hannah Geist, played by Sarah Gadon.

8
00:48:53,333 --> 00:48:59,333
Dr. Abendroth, played by Malcolm McDowell.

9
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Arvid, played by Joe Pingue.

10
01:01:06,666 --> 01:01:12,666
Dev Harvey, played by Sheila McCarthy.

11
01:07:13,333 --> 01:07:19,333
Edward Porris, played by Douglas Smith.

12
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
Antiviral is a 2012 science fiction horror film
written and directed by Brandon Cronenberg.

13
01:19:26,666 --> 01:19:32,666
The film competed in the Un Certain Regard section
at the 2012 Cannes Film Festival.

14
01:25:33,333 --> 01:25:39,333
Cronenberg re-edited the film after the festival to make it
tighter, trimming nearly six minutes out of the film.

15
01:31:40,000 --> 01:31:46,000
The revised film was first shown at the 2012 Toronto International Film Festival, and was a co-winner,
alongside Jason Buxton's Blackbird, of the festival's Best Canadian First Feature Film award.

16
01:37:46,666 --> 01:37:52,666
The film explores themes of future, satire, celebrity, injection, metamorphosis.

17
01:43:53,333 --> 01:43:59,333
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
